  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed on Sunday, June 17, 2007, at Farm Sanctuary in Watkins Glen, NY [1]. This event is the 110th show in the Internet Archive’s collection for the band [4]. The recording, uploaded by mrgrundy, captures 23 songs over 90 minutes [1]. The uploader notes that while they were initially alone on the balcony, ten other people joined them by the time the set began, contributing to some background noise [1]. A listener named cerpntaxt mentioned background conversations but found the audio mostly fine [2]. Another listener, dellegazze, called it one of the best recordings they had heard, noting it was a bit quiet but top-rate [3]. The setlist includes “Leaving home,” which is the only archived performance of this song [1]. “Cao Dai Blowout” and “Red River Valley” are also unique to this archive entry [1]. Several songs are bustouts, such as “Alpha Rats Nest,” which had not appeared in 49 archived shows [1]. “Weekend in western Illinois” is rare, with only 12 archived performances [1]. “Store” is split into two parts, both marking a bustout after 57 shows [1]. “Solomon Revisited” is a bustout after 103 shows and is rare with five archived performances [1]. The set closes with “California Song,” which dellegazze highlighted for the audience singing along [3].",
